# **3.  Chip ****&**** Badge Color System — v36.3 Design Standard**

All chips, pills, and badges site-wide follow a single semantic color vocabulary. Color encodes meaning — not workspace, not feature. All chips use a 2px border.

| **Role** | **CSS Class** | **Color** | **Hex** | **When to Use** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Freeman Now** | .chip-now | Cobalt | #C2D8F8 / #1A40A6 | Freeman Now platform identifier only. |
| **Freeman Next** | .chip-info | Cyan | #00BDF6 | Freeman Next platform, workspace/topic labels, informational category chips. |
| **Success / Complete** | .chip-green | Green | #42BB37 | Task complete, plan confirmed, on track, approved. |
| **Due Next / KPI Near** | .chip-amber | Gold | #FFB500 | Next step in process (no deadline), KPI Near Goal. |
| **Due Today / Urgent** | .chip-urgent | Orange | #FB471F | Task due today, Action Required, Rejected/Denied. |
| **Overdue / KPI Below** | .chip-overdue | Deep Red | #C0001A | Past deadline, KPI Below Goal. Intentionally non-brand for clarity. |
| **Location** | .chip-location | Fuchsia | #FF0373 | Branch, region, or scope on Needs Attention cards. Location only. |
| **Stage / Phase / Type** | .chip-stage | Ghost | transparent | Pipeline stages, phases, type labels, attributes. |

# **4.  Needs Attention Card Structure — Universal Rule**

Every card in the Needs Attention panel follows the same structure regardless of source workspace. All three home page columns use fixed 110px card height with justify-content: space-between and CSS ellipsis truncation on meta lines.

| **Title** | Specific task or action name. white-space:nowrap; overflow:hidden; text-overflow:ellipsis. |
| --- | --- |
| **Supporting line** | Task description if one exists, blank if not. Truncated to one line with ellipsis. |
| **Status pill** | Due Next (amber) → Due Today (orange) → Overdue (red). Priority wins. One pill only. |
| **Topic pill** | Workspace name in cyan (Recruiting, Onboarding, Timekeeping, etc.) |
| **Location pill** | Branch or scope in fuchsia (Nashville, Enterprise, Las Vegas, etc.) |
| **Chip rows** | flex-wrap: nowrap — chips never break to a second line. |

# **5.  Active Events Card Structure — v36.6 Design Standard**

| **Title row** | Show name + separator + Job # (cyan, bold). |
| --- | --- |
| **Meta line** | Venue/facility · Date range (Mon DD – Mon DD) · Booth count. Single line, ellipsis truncation. |
| **Platform chip** | Freeman Now (cobalt) or Freeman Next (cyan). |
| **No branch** | Location context comes from venue name — no producing branch on card. |
| **Date format** | "Mon DD – Mon DD" with en-dash. No "Move-in" or "Clear" labels. |

# **6.  KPI Tile Design — v36.13 Design Standard**

| **Metric name** | Uppercase, bold, muted gray. Top of card. |
| --- | --- |
| **Current value** | Large (28px bold), Freeman Blue (#001F5F). Dominant visual. |
| **Goal label** | "Goal: X%" — regular weight, muted gray (#7A8099). Not bold. |
| **Status pill** | Floated right on goal line. Green (Exceeds Goal), Gold (Meets Goal), Red (Below Goal). No arrows. |
| **Progress bar** | Removed in v36.13. |

# **7.  Recruiting ****&**** Hiring — ES Date Gate (v36.10 / v36.20)**

The hiring cycle for all open positions is controlled by two enterprise-level dates set by Craig Gaibler or Nesana Wieger: the next ES Start Date and the next ES NET Class date. These are not per-hire checklist items — they are the starting gun that unlocks all open positions simultaneously.

## **How the cycle works**

| **1** | Open positions accumulate on the R&H board as roles become available (offboards, transitions, new approvals). They are visible but frozen. |
| --- | --- |
| **2** | While either date is TBD, every position's checklist shows a locked state: padlock icon + "Awaiting confirmed start dates." |
| **3** | Craig or Nesana clicks "Set Next ES Start Date" or "Set Next ES NET Class" and enters a date via modal. |
| **4** | When both dates are confirmed, saveEsDate() auto-checks t0a and t0b on ALL open hire records simultaneously. |
| **5** | If either date is reset to TBD, t0a and t0b are automatically unchecked on all open records. |
| **6** | New hire records (manual, TR backfill, OFF backfill) call rhInitialChecked() — born with t0a/t0b pre-checked if dates are already set. |
| **7** | Three weeks after NET Class date passes, both dates reset to TBD, triggering the next cycle. |

## **Architecture notes**

t0a and t0b are enterprise-level triggers only — NOT included in any hire record's TASK_STAGE_MAP. renderNeedsAttention() checks esDateGet() directly. renderDetail() gates the checklist on date state.

