# **12.  Employee Lifecycle Architecture**

All four Employee Lifecycle pages (Recruiting & Hiring, Onboarding, Transitions, Offboarding) share an identical det-split layout for their detail panels. This is the non-negotiable structural standard.

## **det-split layout — universal structure**

| **.det-sticky** | Pinned identity card at top. Never scrolls. Contains avatar, role │ name, meta line, chips, date pill, progress bar, and optional Revise button (top-right). |
| --- | --- |
| **.det-process-label** | Section divider line with process name ("Recruiting & Hiring Process", "Offboarding Process", etc.) |
| **.det-scroll** | Independently scrolling task list + backfill bar + close bar below. |

## **Sequential process rule**

Every process is a strict ordered sequence. Only the globally-next unchecked task in the sequence is "live." The person responsible for that step gets a Needs Attention card. Nobody downstream gets notified until their turn arrives.

## **Process flow — close → backfill**

When a Transition (Transfer Out) or Offboarding record is closed with backfill approved, a new hire record is automatically created on the Recruiting & Hiring board. The new record calls rhInitialChecked() to determine its starting state based on whether ES dates are already confirmed.

## **Offboarding processes**

| **Process** | **Steps** | **Notes** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Resignation | 13 | Step 2 (Submit Offboarding Service Request) owned by ES Administrator (Erii Rodriguez). |
| Termination | 14 | Step 2 (Grant or Deny Approval) owned by ES Leadership. Step 6 (Submit Service Request) owned by ES Administrator. |

# **13.  Global Design Rules — Non-Negotiable**

| **Rule** | **Detail** |
| --- | --- |
| **No strikethrough — ever** | Done states use muted color (var(--muted)) + filled green checkbox ONLY. text-decoration:line-through is NEVER used anywhere on the site — task lists, process steps, PM steps, or any other context. Violation of this rule will be corrected immediately. |
| **No color-coded identity cards for TR/OFF** | Transitions and Offboarding identity cards use Freeman Blue (var(--mb)) for the top bar, avatar, and progress bar — identical to RH, OB, PM, and Staffing. No gold or orange on structural card elements. Color-coded chips are acceptable; card structure is always blue. |
| **No overdue tracking on TR/OFF** | Transitions and Offboarding are open-ended sequential workflows with no per-step deadlines. Track chip shows "In Progress" or "Complete" only. Overdue tracking is exclusive to Recruiting & Hiring. |
| **Task layout: Option A** | On any process page with both descriptions and links: title on top → brief description below → "Additional details ↗" pill on its own line. Never inline, never between title and description. |
| **Task copy style** | All task description copy: remove unnecessary "the" articles; replace "and" with "&". Keeps descriptions concise. |
| **Section labels on all pages** | Every page begins its content area with an el-section-div label. Employee Lifecycle / Team Operations / Service Excellence pages: "By the Numbers". Lens pages: "[Name] Search". Matches "Welcome" and "Current KPIs" on their respective pages. |
| **No page subtitles** | Page subtitles removed site-wide in v36.34 — redundant with page title and scope pills already visible in the nav. Coming Soon pages and the Today's Priorities date stamp are exceptions. |
| **Sequential NA card rule** | Needs Attention surfaces only the globally-next unchecked task per record, to the identity who owns that exact step. No cards for steps blocked by incomplete prior steps. Applies to needsMyAction() (RH), lcNeedsAction() (OB/TR/OFF), and the RH NA render block. |
| **Pre-push validation** | All code changes are validated for: (1) JS syntax via node Function() parse, and (2) HTML div balance across all 20 page divs. A broken div balance causes all pages to bleed into each other. Both checks must pass before any commit. |
| **Welcome panel height** | 150px min-height. This is the confirmed final value after multiple adjustments on 2026-05-22. |

